rks an ongoing passive action.","keywords":["continuous-passive"],"skill":"continuous-passive","contextKey":"passive-voice-2","fingerprint":"ade53987c2e9922da144bae29efe86eb0248a6d77ef0cbd6399f567b9b902b35","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-passives"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Ongoing passive = **be + being + past participle**.","After the finite form of be, **being restored** marks an ongoing passive action.","Choose **being restored**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"This makes simple passive, not the requested continuous passive.","B":"The passive part needs a past participle after being.","C":"After the finite form of be, **being restored** marks an ongoing passive action.","D":"Been belongs after perfect have, not directly after is."}}},{"id":"ac28dadd-b61a-5b9c-a9a0-fe931b1ee5db","topicSlug":"passive-voice","level":"B1","prompt":"Use a modal passive: “The old portrait must ____ before Friday.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"be restoring"},{"id":"B","text":"be restored"},{"id":"C","text":"been restored"},{"id":"D","text":"is restored"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"The object receives the required action: **must be + participle**.","explanation":"After must, use base **be** and participle **restored**.","keywords":["modal-passive"],"skill":"modal-passive","contextKey":"passive-voice-2","fingerprint":"f4a6df4cd1651c9bde9785966af69f3d2b1af857c251b1e6b2e834c59f6bb9fd","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-passives"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The object receives the required action: **must be + participle**.","After must, use base **be** and participle **restored**.","Choose **be restored**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"This is active continuous, not passive.","B":"After must, use base **be** and participle **restored**.","C":"Must needs have before been; this task asks for a simple modal passive.","D":"A finite is cannot follow must."}}},{"id":"5704e32c-a26c-52ce-a138-ae573aae4c96","topicSlug":"passive-voice","level":"B1","prompt":"Use present simple passive: “The garden fence ____ every week.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"is measured"},{"id":"B","text":"is measuring"},{"id":"C","text":"are measured"},{"id":"D","text":"is to measure"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"The task asks for **receiver + present be + past participle**.","explanation":"The singular/uncountable subject takes **is**, followed by participle **measured**.","keywords":["present-passive"],"skill":"present-passive","contextKey":"passive-voice-3","fingerprint":"32424a81d955c0d1a83422bea7bafb256a11f069feef36b7de1788de9dd5aee6","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-passives"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The task asks for **receiver + present be + past participle**.","The singular/uncountable subject takes **is**, followed by participle **measured**.","Choose **is measured**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The singular/uncountable subject takes **is**, followed by participle **measured**.","B":"This is active continuous, not passive.","C":"This form of be does not agree with the subject.","D":"This is not the present-simple passive construction."}}},{"id":"a66b9b6f-a4f6-5d73-a3e9-293df410ce7b","topicSlug":"passive-voice","level":"B1","prompt":"Use past simple passive: “The garden fence ____ yesterday.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"was measuring"},{"id":"B","text":"did measured"},{"id":"C","text":"was measured"},{"id":"D","text":"were measured"}],"answerId":"C